Name: stopListening

Type: command

Syntax: stopListening

Summary:
Stops the speech recognition engine immediately. No further <voiceCommand>,
<wakeWordDetected>, or <listenTimeoutExpired> messages will be dispatched
until <startListening> is called again.

Introduced: 1.0.0

OS: mac, Windows, Linux

Platforms: desktop

Example:
-- Stop listening when we no longer need voice commands
stopListening

Example:
-- Clean up when the application quits
on shutdownApp
    stopListening
    unregisterAllVoiceCommands
end shutdownApp

Description:
Use <stopListening> to release the microphone and stop all speech
recognition activity. Registered command phrases are retained — calling
<startListening> again will resume recognition of the same phrases
without needing to re-register them.

Calling <stopListening> when the engine is not running is a no-op.

References: startListening (command), isListening (function),
registerVoiceCommand (command), unregisterAllVoiceCommands (command)

Tags: speech, voice
